{"anchor": {"begin": [128, 0, 287.33], "end": [128, 0, 399.33], "env": "corollary", "file": null, "head": null, "id": 60, "kind": "approximate", "label": null, "labels": [], "line": null, "number": "A.3", "source_sha256": "6009a34d604e68f5a278172da4266fede06e7b2d0daf3568175365758943053d", "statement": "Corollary A.3. Use the five radial moment functions (M, I, J, S, C p ) of (4.15), where C p is the pressure increment. Under X = ρ x their normalizing factors are ( ρ , ρ 3/2 , ρ 3/2 , ρ , 1), H = ρ 1/2 √ 2xE. (A.4) On a fixed correction interval suppose U 0 = u c ( η ) and E 0 = e ∗ f ∗ ( η )xα, with e ∗ > 0 and smooth f ∗ > 0. Two additive U bumps and three additive E bumps give an invertible Jacobian of the normalized five-moment map provided α / ∈ {−1/2, 1/2, 3/2}. The moment changes have the exact quadratic form (A.2). At U 0 = 0, the three corrections to E can prescribe changes in (I, S, C p ) while preserving M, J.", "title": null}, "blockers": [], "class": "proved", "clauses": [], "correspondence": {"by": "Christian Garry (drafted with Claude Code)", "confidence": "medium", "coverage": "partial", "note": "Invertibility of the Jacobian of the five moments (M, I, J, S, Cp) for U = G constant, E = A·x^b with A ≠ 0 and b ∉ {−1/2, 1/2, 3/2}, two U bumps and three E bumps, and the exact linear-plus-quadratic form (A.2), are stated. The normalizing factors (A.4) under X = ρx and the assertion that at U0 = 0 the three E corrections prescribe (I, S, Cp) while preserving M, J have no counterpart.", "source": "confirmed"}, "decls": {"NavierStokes.FiveProfileMoments.Coeff": "d3025260d925bad0ecfac738", "NavierStokes.FiveProfileMoments.Debt": "a3e0df8946a7d58600cd37dd", "NavierStokes.FiveProfileMoments.GoodExponent": "5f099dae663090fa71173b45", "NavierStokes.FiveProfileMoments.Patch": "cdd31b5a616d115f0a0d9e32", "NavierStokes.FiveProfileMoments.Patch.left": "7a2d1c0fe21c7a6f92977829", "NavierStokes.FiveProfileMoments.Patch.leftHalf": "90918b1341f06ff2cae54f4f", "NavierStoke